<title>USA: Compaq wins BZW workstation contract.</title>
<headline>Compaq wins BZW workstation contract.</headline>
<dateline>HOUSTON 1997-03-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Compaq Computer Corp said Wednesday it won a contract from BZW to sell 5,700 Compaq professional workstations.</p>
<p>The contract from BZW, a UK-based global investment bank of the Barclays Group, also includes several thousand Compaq monitors as well as 80 Compaq servers, the company said.</p>
<p>Terms of the contract were not disclosed. Roll-out will take place from February 1997 to August 1997.</p>
<p>The Compaq work stations and monitors, to be used in both the trading environment and the general office, will run Microsoft NT operating system.</p>
</text>
